  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 349 AM MDT THU MAY 28 2026\nSunday will mark the start of a warming and drying trend as the\nupper-low exits our area. A weak shortwave will immediately \nfollow this exiting low, but it looks inconsequential for our \narea. The best chance of precipitation throughout the long term \nwill come Sunday in our far northeastern zones, where isolated \nshowers may persist across higher terrain on the back side of \nthe exiting low. Ridging will begin to build into the area come \nMonday, supporting a warming trend through the week. \nTemperatures on Sunday will sit right around normal, warming to \n10-15 degrees above normal by Wednesday.",
